WITH blk(lang, k, html, more, nextlen) AS (VALUES
  ('en', 1, '<p><strong>Sales Order</strong></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
  ('en', 2, '<p><b>Before you start.</b> These must exist first: Target Document Type (<b>Document Type</b>), <b>Business Partner</b>, Partner Location (<b>Business Partner</b>), Warehouse (<b>Warehouse and Locators</b>), <b>Price List</b>, Sales Representative (<b>User</b>), <b>Payment Term</b>.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
  ('en', 3, '<p><b>Do it.</b> Fill <b>Order</b>, then <b>Order Line</b>, <b>Order Tax</b>, <b>Payment Schedule</b>, <b>POS Payment</b>; then the Document Action <b>Complete</b>.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
  ('en', 4, '<p><b>What Complete does.</b></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
  ('en', 5, '<ul><li>On Credit Order, Warehouse Order, POS Order (Prepay Order if <i>Generate Shipment</i>): also creates and completes the shipment ✓</li><li>POS Order, On Credit Order (Prepay Order if <i>Generate Invoice</i>): also creates the invoice ✓</li><li>Standard Order: reserves the ordered quantity; shipment and invoice are made next ✓</li><li>Quotation: reserves the quantity and creates nothing else</li><li>Proposal: reserves nothing and creates nothing else</li><li>Prepay Order: waits for a payment (status Waiting Payment)</li><li>The next action offered is Close</li></ul>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
  ('en', 6, '<p><b>When it refuses</b>, legacy says: “Period Closed” ✓; “Product is not on Price List” ✓; “Business Partner with this Order over Credit Hold” ✓; “Fill mandatory fields: Shipper”; “No Document Lines found”; “Product … Exclude Auto Delivery”; “Line No … - Invalid: Date Promised”; “Cannot change Document Type”; “Cannot reserve Stock”; “Error calculating tax”; “Error in payment schedule”.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
  ('en', 7, '<p><i>Read from iDempiere''s MOrder.java and the dictionary. ✓ = seen in a legacy run of 2026-11-23.</i></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 120),
  ('en', 8, '<p><strong>1 · Sales Order</strong></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERPUserGuide/#1-sales-order" target="_blank">1 · Sales Order …</a></p>', 120),
  ('en', 9, '<p>Open <b><b>Sales Order</b></b> from the menu (⌂ → Sales), create a line or two, and press the <b>Process</b> button (§6) → <b>Complete</b>. Completion is not just a status flip: <code>completeIt</code> fans out into the shipment and invoice that follow it, in the SAME signed op-group.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERPUserGuide/#1-sales-order" target="_blank">1 · Sales Order …</a></p>', 154),
  ('en', 10, '<p><strong>Step 7 · Enter the order header</strong></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-7-enter-the-order-header" target="_blank">Step 7 · Enter the order header …</a></p>', 154),
  ('en', 11, '<ol><li value="1">Open <b><b>Sales Order</b></b> (window 143) and click <b>New record</b>.</li><li value="2"><b><b>Business Partner</b></b>: e.g. <i>Joe Block</i>. Choosing it fills <b>Invoice Partner</b> and <b><b>Price List</b></b> automatically (<code>CalloutOrder.bPartner</code>, logged).</li><li value="3"><b>Target Document Type</b>: <b>Standard Order</b>.</li><li value="4">Click <b>Save</b>.</li></ol>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-7-enter-the-order-header" target="_blank">Step 7 · Enter the order header …</a></p>', 146),
  ('en', 12, '<p><strong>Step 9 · Complete the order</strong></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-9-complete-the-order" target="_blank">Step 9 · Complete the order …</a></p>', 146),
  ('en', 13, '<ol><li value="1">Go back to the <b><b>Order</b></b> tab. Your order is still the selected record, so there is nothing to look up in the list.</li><li value="2">The form shows the actions that are allowed now: <b>Complete · Prepare · Void</b>. Click <b>Complete</b>.</li></ol>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-9-complete-the-order" target="_blank">Step 9 · Complete the order …</a></p>', 146),
  ('en', 14, '<p>The status becomes <b>Completed (CO)</b>. The change is stored as a signed entry, and the chain check passes (<code>§CRUD process committed … to=CO verifyChain=ok</code>). <b>Reload the page and it is still CO.</b></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-9-complete-the-order" target="_blank">Step 9 · Complete the order …</a></p>', 146),
  ('en', 15, '<p><b>What Complete creates depends on the document type, exactly as in iDempiere.</b> A <b>Standard Order</b> creates nothing else on Complete: its shipment and invoice come later (iDempiere''s <i>Generate Shipments</i> / <i>Generate Invoices</i>). A <b>POS Order</b>, <b>Warehouse Order</b> or <b>Credit Order</b> creates its shipment on Complete, and a POS or Credit Order also its invoice.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-9-complete-the-order" target="_blank">Step 9 · Complete the order …</a></p>', 146),
  ('en', 16, '<p>Those documents are full documents you can open (<b><b>Shipment (Customer)</b></b>, <b>Invoice (Customer)</b>): customer, document type, lines, prices and totals are copied from the order. They are then <b>posted</b> to the books, the way iDempiere''s accounting processor posts completed documents: the invoice debits <i>Accounts Receivable</i> and credits <i>Revenue</i> (and <i>Tax Due</i> when there is tax); the shipment debits <i>Cost of Goods Sold</i> and credits <i>Product Asset</i> at the product''s current average cost.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERP_FirstSetup/#step-9-complete-the-order" target="_blank">Step 9 · Complete the order …</a></p>', 0),
  ('de_DE', 1, '<p><strong>1 · Auftrag</strong></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERPUserGuide/#1-sales-order" target="_blank">1 · Auftrag …</a></p>', 116),
  ('de_DE', 2, '<p>Öffnen Sie <b><b>Auftrag</b></b> im Menü (⌂ → Vertrieb), legen Sie eine oder zwei Positionen an und drücken Sie die Schaltfläche <b>Verarbeiten</b> (§6) → <b>Fertigstellen</b>. Fertigstellen ist mehr als ein Statuswechsel: <code>completeIt</code> erzeugt die folgende Lieferung und Rechnung in DERSELBEN signierten Operationsgruppe.</p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/ERPUserGuide/#1-sales-order" target="_blank">1 · Auftrag …</a></p>', 113),
  ('de_DE', 3, '<p><strong>Sales Order</strong></p>', '<p><a href="https://red1oon.github.io/BIMCompiler/LegacyOracleAdapterSpec/" target="_blank">Sales Order …</a></p>', 113),
